{"kind":"request","text":"LP-1: Lending declares its publication paths.\n\nFinding, read in source at main 863ca6b2. Each Lending act sends\n`publish-file` to the Library's destination (`examples/lending/\ndefinition.json`). The package declares no capability:\n`examples/lending/dap.application.json` has `\"capabilities\": []`. In\na `base` room the Directory then gives the Destination an empty\nprefix list (`base-directory.ts:110-115`), and Destination 21 refuses\neach `publish-file` with `publication-path-not-declared`\n(`base-destination.ts:68-73`). An installed Lending 0.2.0 Library\npublishes no shelf page. The source has no uninstall, and a later\nrelease does not change the prefixes of an earlier installation.\n\nSo I do not install Lending 0.2.0 in the room `lending-library`.\nThat corrects my act 58bcabf2. The room waits for a release that\npublishes.\n\nWork:\n1. Test first. In a `base` room, install the current Lending package\n   and donate one thing. Show what the Destination answers to the\n   `publish-file` of that act. If the page is published today, stop\n   and tell me: my reading is then wrong.\n2. Declare `publication-paths@1` in the Lending package with the\n   prefixes of the pages that the definition sends. Use the fewest\n   prefixes that cover them.\n3. The same test then shows the published page and its receipt.\n4. State in the Lending README what a Library publishes and where.\n\nLimits. The change rides the open Lending 0.3.0 and changes its\nidentifiers with no question, under 163de663. Counter is out of\nscope: tell me in one line whether Counter sends `publish-file`.\n\nOrder. LP-1 can ride R's head or land as its own head before R.\nChoose the cheaper one and say which. It lands before I sign Lending\n0.3.0. After the signing, a small head adds the 0.3.0 packet, its\nrow and the screen host row of the installed Library.\n\nNF-7 is free to start. The deployment of 58bcabf2 gave `dap-lending`\nthe Counter row and the content bucket. The Counter witness also\nproves the hosted path for a packet of 2.6 MB. Run it outside a gate.","body":{"conditions":"The head lands on main with the gate passed and the checker's approval. The Lending package declares publication-paths@1. A test in a base room shows that an act of an installed Library publishes its page at the Destination.","target_head":"863ca6b2ee23c528af97b352165092c556ca35f9","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}